Peter Baucom the platform lead at  Quizlet Inc said we believe GCP has  better core technology in particular  it's networking and disk technology  thanks Peter we really appreciate that a  huge component of why that may be is  Google's persistent disk persistent  disks are durable network storage  devices that your instances can access  like physical disks in a desktop or  server the data on each persistent disk  is distributed across several physical  disks compute engine manages the  physical disks and the data distribution  to ensure redundancy and optimize  performance for you  persistent disk offers multi reader  capability with multi reader mounting  many virtual machines can read data from  a single persistent disk with no  performance degradation multi reader  mounting makes sharing content a snap  this lab will take you about 30 minutes  to complete and you'll learn how to  create a virtual machine instance create  a new persistent disk attach persistent  disks to a virtual machine instance  format and mount the persistent disk and  automatically mount the disk on restart  persistent disks are located  independently from your virtual machine  instances so you can detach or move  persistent disks to keep your data even  after you delete your instances this is  the fifth lab in the GCP essentials  quest completing this quest earns you  this patch to recognize your achievement  next up hello node keeper Nettie's
 

